WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.535
-Our next guest is a
Tony-nominated actor

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:05.204
you know from films like
"American Hustle," "Selma,"

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:06.439
and "A Most Violent Year."

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.041
He stars in
"The Many Saints of Newark,"

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.076
which is in theaters and
available on HBO Max now.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.377
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:14.313
-You know I don't like to lean
on you about stuff.

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:17.083
But you can't start
a gambling operation at school.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:20.052
-I know that...now.

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:22.888
-Don't [ Bleep ] me.
You always knew it.

00:00:22.888 --> 00:00:24.824
It's not just the gambling.
It's everything.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.093
The cherry bombs at the YMCA.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.661
Letting the air out of
Mrs. Russo's tires.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.062
-I apologized to her!
-You talk big

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:31.698
about wanting to be on the
football team in high school,

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.432
and you're smoking already?
Oh!

00:00:33.432 --> 00:00:35.401
You got to have
a better attitude.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:37.803
With your father gone,

00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:39.005
your mother's got
a lot on her plate.

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.839
You got to be good.

00:00:40.839 --> 00:00:43.043
I don't want to have to
go through this again.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:46.845
-I try to be good.
-I don't think so.

00:00:46.845 --> 00:00:49.482
-Please welcome to the show
Alessandro Nivola.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:52.918
[ Applause ]

00:00:52.918 --> 00:00:54.387
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.955
-Oh.
-That's a very good "oh."

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.924
It's a very good.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:00.693
♪♪

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.929
Thank you so much for being here
and in the studio.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.764
How are you?
-I'm good.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.232
-So this is --
-Thanks for having me.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.967
-It's so exciting to be
back in this world.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.369
It's a prequel.
So, obviously, you weren't

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:13.139
in "The Sopranos," which is
a New Jersey show,

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.542
but, you know, for an actor
in New York, especially,

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.577
you know, I feel like
when that came out,

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:19.311
that was the show
for actors in New York.

00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:20.713
Were you in New York City
at the time?

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.582
Were you living here?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:25.618
I was living --
I was living in the Village.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:28.087
I live in Brooklyn now,
but I was living in --

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.323
on Christopher Street, which --
-Alright!

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.225
I used to live on Christopher.
-Did you?

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:33.426
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-You're kidding me?

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:36.029
Where? Between 7th and Bleecker?
That was my --

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.663
-Yes. Yep, yeah.
-So you know the block.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:40.033
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-So, I was living in, like,

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:43.536
a tiny little studio apartment.
There was, you know, my bathtub

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.972
was in my living room.
-Uh-huh.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:50.877
-And across the street was
"Tony n' Tina's Wedding."

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.111
You know, the church
where Tony and Tina...

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:56.082
People who are
not from New York,

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:57.617
don't know what
"Tony n' Tina's Wedding" is.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:01.820
But, it's like, you pay
to be part of, like,

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:04.357
"My Big Fat Italian Wedding"
or whatever.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.392
And you go,
you watch this wedding,

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.560
and then they get in a fight
during the wedding,

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.596
and they spill out
onto the street.

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:12.498
And they're all, like,
yelling at each other.

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:13.666
And you know,
there's somebody --

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:16.535
a woman saying like,
"Vinny, you worm!

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:20.106
I did it with Mario, Vinny!
I did it with Mario!"

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:23.409
[ Laughter ]
And then, like, underneath me

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:27.546
was a gay leather bar
called Boots &amp; Saddle.

00:02:27.546 --> 00:02:28.982
-Uh-huh.
-And those guys --

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:32.684
these big bearded guys were
sitting there at the counter,

00:02:32.684 --> 00:02:35.954
just, like, staring out
at "Tony n' Tina's Wedding"

00:02:35.954 --> 00:02:37.423
like four times a day,

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:39.726
watching her talk
about doing it with Mario.

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:42.061
[ Laughter ]
That was my life.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.530
-That's New York City
in a nutshell, right there.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:47.600
-Yeah, yeah.
-So, you got cast in this.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.335
And obviously,
it was a big deal.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.704
I think people were waiting
for this for a long time.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.405
Your family
must have been excited

00:02:53.405 --> 00:02:55.808
that you got this part.
-Yeah.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:59.445
Well, I -- You know, my --
So, my brother --

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:02.615
I think the day
that I got cast,

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:05.818
I got this text from him
saying like,

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.620
"You're not gonna believe this,

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.624
but I was watching season 2,

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.326
episode something or other,

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:16.462
and it's an episode
where they all went to Italy

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.931
to, like, get in touch
with the motherland, you know."

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:20.933
-Yep.
-And, of course,

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:22.301
everyone in Italy, like, thinks

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:24.003
they're a bunch of idiots
or whatever.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:26.672
Not the reception
that they'd hoped for.

00:03:26.672 --> 00:03:30.242
But there's this scene,
and he's watching it,

00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:33.646
and James Gandolfini's face
is in close-up.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:36.048
There it is.
-That's the still, right there.

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:40.353
-So, in the back of the scene
is this sculpture.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.520
-There's a better photo
of the sculpture.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.489
-Yeah, that's this sculpture.
This --

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:46.959
So, my grandfather
made this sculpture.

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:49.229
And he's a sculptor,

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:51.030
and there happened to be
some exhibition

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.100
of his stuff in Naples,
where they were filming.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.235
And you know, the guy
who was directing it

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:59.772
liked the look of it,
and he shot the scene.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:03.175
And there it was,
in the back of the scene.

00:04:03.175 --> 00:04:06.679
I called up David Chase
and told him, like, you know,

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.881
"My granddad's sculpture
is in your show."

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.050
And he was -- he was spooked,
you know.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:14.320
-Yeah, so, I talked to David
Chase the other day,

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.389
and I bet that he was
kind of, like, "Okay."

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:20.059
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:22.561
-No, this actually
got a rise out of him.

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:23.696
-Oh, that's good.
-He's like --

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.631
He gets freaked out
by, sort of, ghosts.

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:26.965
-Okay, that's good to know.
Yeah.

00:04:26.965 --> 00:04:29.168
He doesn't seem like a man
who is easily freaked out.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.871
-No, he definitely doesn't
give too much away.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:34.374
-So, your grandfather was
an artist, as you mentioned,

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:36.808
and friends with another artist.

00:04:36.808 --> 00:04:39.211
So, that -- that's
Jackson Pollock.

00:04:39.211 --> 00:04:40.380
-Yeah.
-And so your --

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.847
So, your grandfather
was friends with him.

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:46.719
-Yeah, so he moved out --
he was living in the Village.

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:48.855
He came from Sardinia
during the war,

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:51.023
and he was living
in Greenwich Village.

00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:54.760
And you know, it's part of that
kind of Bohemian scene there.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:57.263
In fact, he was friends
with De Niro's dad.

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:58.931
-Wow.
-Everybody thinks that De Niro

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:02.835
is, like, the tough guy
from the mean streets.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.637
But he was, like,
the son of an artist

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:07.173
living in the Village
and -- just like my dad.

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:11.510
And then, in the '50s,
my grandfather moved

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.145
out to Long Island

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:15.615
to this area where a lot of
artists lived out there.

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:18.684
In fact, so, Pollock
was living there

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:21.721
and de Kooning -- all these guys
who are famous now.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:25.558
But at the time, they were just,
you know, hanging out together,

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:28.828
getting drunk, and talking
about politics or whatever.

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:31.096
And they used to
give each other art.

00:05:31.096 --> 00:05:35.301
And Pollock
gave my grandfather --

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:38.170
Yeah, this is -- okay.
Pollock gave this painting,

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:40.639
right there,
to my grandfather.

00:05:40.639 --> 00:05:43.875
And he put it on the wall
in the house --

00:05:43.875 --> 00:05:45.244
that's their house --

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:48.380
and he sat there like that
for about a week, I'm told.

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.316
And he just, sort of, you know,
stared at it.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.885
And at the end of the week,

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:55.488
he took it down
and he gave it back.

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:57.690
And apparently he said,

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:03.729
[Italian accent] "Jackson,
I cannot keep this painting.

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:07.300
It makes me nervous."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.770
"Whenever the children play
in the room with the painting,

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.405
they fight."

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:13.605
[ Normal voice ]
And so he gave it back,

00:06:13.605 --> 00:06:15.173
and he took -- you know,
Pollock was like,

00:06:15.173 --> 00:06:16.642
"Yeah, you know --"
he took it

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.210
and, like, shoved it off
someplace.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.912
-So he just thought it had,
like, a bad energy.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:21.714
-Well, no, he just, like,
I don't know --

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:23.716
it didn't have the fêng shui
or whatever.

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:27.686
And I then was at MoMA
like a few years ago.

00:06:27.686 --> 00:06:30.223
They did a retrospective
on Pollock's work.

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:32.291
[ Chuckles ]
And I saw the painting.

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:34.426
And I'd, like, seen that picture
a million times,

00:06:34.426 --> 00:06:35.761
'cause my family had it.

00:06:35.761 --> 00:06:38.731
And I was like, "Wait a minute,
that's the picture."

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:40.566
And sure enough,
that was the painting.

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:41.934
And I looked it up,

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:45.104
and it sold at auction
for $25 million.

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:46.705
-You should have --
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.705 --> 00:06:48.975
Yeah, but the people
who bought it said,

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:50.710
like, their kids fight.
It's not worth it.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:51.811
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:53.745
-It was a deal with the devil.
-Yeah.

00:06:53.745 --> 00:06:55.414
You should have gone up at MoMA
and been like,

00:06:55.414 --> 00:06:57.883
"This is so awkward.
That's my painting."

00:06:57.883 --> 00:07:00.019
[ Laughter ]
-I wouldn't have had to have

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:02.121
been living across
from "Tony n' Tina's Wedding"

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:04.423
if I had cashed in.
-You did some --

00:07:04.423 --> 00:07:06.325
So, you went to Newark,
and you did some --

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:07.894
It was very cool.

00:07:07.894 --> 00:07:10.762
You did some research
for the part.

00:07:10.762 --> 00:07:15.767
Did you find this picture
of a young -- young Joe Pesci?

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:19.472
Where'd you find this photo?
-Well, there's a museum

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:22.908
in the basement of
Saint Lucy's Church in Newark,

00:07:22.908 --> 00:07:25.944
And it's the history of
the whole neighborhood,

00:07:25.944 --> 00:07:27.947
of all the Italian part
of Newark.

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:29.382
It's called the First Ward.

00:07:29.382 --> 00:07:33.286
And in there are, like, old
pictures that nobody else has.

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:35.354
They're actually -- They're not
like, reproduced pictures.

00:07:35.354 --> 00:07:37.089
They're actual photos
on the wall

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:38.824
that people have just given
over the years.

00:07:38.824 --> 00:07:40.493
And there's everybody there.

00:07:40.493 --> 00:07:42.594
You know, I mean,
Sinatra and all these guys.

00:07:42.594 --> 00:07:45.931
But there's
this picture of Pesci.

00:07:45.931 --> 00:07:47.566
That's Pesci.

00:07:47.566 --> 00:07:50.269
And he was in a band
called the Zaniacs,

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:54.941
which were also known
as the Zani Acts.

00:07:54.941 --> 00:07:57.042
-Oh, yeah. There you go.
Now you get it, yeah.

00:07:57.042 --> 00:07:59.945
-And they had backup singers
called the Yum Yum girls.

00:07:59.945 --> 00:08:01.247
-Yeah.
-There they are.

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:03.115
-And that was him.
-Joe Pesci, you kind of think,

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:05.150
"What would young Joe Pesci
look like?"

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:06.485
And then you're like, "Yeah,
he'd look like that."

00:08:06.485 --> 00:08:07.953
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.953 --> 00:08:09.355
-He had some great hair
in those days.

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:11.724
-It's really --
Congrats again on the film.

00:08:11.724 --> 00:08:12.959
-Hey, a pleasure. Thank you.

00:08:12.959 --> 00:08:14.427
-Thanks so much for spending
time with us.

00:08:14.427 --> 00:08:15.828
We really appreciate it.
-Thanks so much.

00:08:15.828 --> 00:08:17.596
Great to see you.
-"The Many Saints of Newark"

00:08:17.596 --> 00:08:19.532
is in theaters now and
also available on HBO Max.

